Subject: Cantor B1 Trusted Time Witness Receipt Verification P0 Requirements Analysis

@ [requirements_uuid] 87994a0a-9193-48aa-8c27-aed5ddd0de32
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 3f33fd16-abed-4838-9272-bc3f44aaff54

& [RequirementPartition]
  + TWV-001 through TWV-006 cover custody bounded forms exact evidence and transitive replay
  + TWV-007 through TWV-016 cover descriptor isolation raw bytes identity key expectations signatures structural bounds comparison and cycle-free lineage
  + TWV-017 through TWV-024 cover request receipt conserved truth strict serialization independent evidence and typed adversaries
  + TWV-025 through TWV-027 cover zero effects research and immutable governance
& [GapsResolved]
  + issued and expiry bounds are inclusive structural bounds; A3 interval endpoints are also included in descriptive within outcome
  + sequence is the source-permitted sequence_or_nonce variant; positive u64 sequence is matched to request but does not prevent replay
  + request supplies expected key label witness identity sequence; changing a complete input request is a new correspondence event not an authentication guarantee
& [Excluded]
  + production currentness revocation decisions live service and authority are not requirements of this bounded implementation
